Z||000008||Fearless Freep||09-14-2000||04:39 PM||||Trick seems to be to keep my foot out the floor and use the cruise as much as possible kind hard when 1/2 of the trip is straight bumper to bumper 5 lane 75+mph interstate beltlines.  I never use anything less than 93oct. Had the exhaust all changed out...planning on putting the pulley and hypertech chip in next weekend.||||reg||1
Z||000009||DJRice||09-14-2000||09:37 PM||||Monkey, <P>Sounds like its time to get the Grape Ape a new set of Bananas!  <P>Seriously, did you give the car a tune up before you started driving it daily?  Maybe a new set of plugs, and filters all the way around.  <P>My V-6 gets about 23-27 mpg depending on the week.<P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>"You mean like the back seat of a Volkswagen?"||||reg||1
Z||000010||Fearless Freep||09-14-2000||10:09 PM||||Dj.....lemme think what I have done....Hmmmm..<P>1. Well every 4000 miles or so I use a  <BR>   fuel/injector cleaner.<BR>2. Accel Coil and Ignition module<BR>3. Bosch Platinum Plus 4 plugs<BR>4. K & N Air filter (due for a charge)<BR>5. Free flowing cat and muffler, pipes<BR>6. New alternator<BR>7. New Fuel pump<P>Next week I will be replacing the pulley and installing the hypertech chip, also will be installing one of those e-ram chargers probably in a month or so for that one.<P>Future upgrade (ie. next 0-3 months)<BR>1. Power Pulley<BR>2. Hypertech chip<BR>3. Front Bushings & Rear bushings<BR>4. 8mm plug wires<BR>5. e-ram electric supercharger<BR>6. Rodney's shortshifter<BR>7. New ported manifolds or Headers<P>and the most important thing.........a new windshield washer pump.<P>Course after all that, it will all crap out on me and I will ship it to Archie for a V8  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
